  <div class="prose">
    <p>I've spent more than 15 years on both sides of building software: writing the code and deciding what's worth writing. I started as an engineer at a Fortune 500 software company, moved into leading incubation teams there, and have been starting and running things of my own ever since.</p>

    <p>Along the way I've been a Chief Product Officer, founded <strong>RowHero</strong> to replace the stopwatch and clipboard for rowing coaches, and now run <strong>Northforge</strong>, where I teach real estate developers, investors, and law firms to use AI in their everyday work. I also host technology and AI tutorials for a YouTube channel with 4.5 million subscribers.</p>

    <p>The common thread is that I care about outcomes more than output. A roadmap matters if the company actually follows it. An AI tool matters if it gives someone their Friday afternoon back. I like being close to the work, close to the people using what I build, and honest about what's working.</p>

    <p>This site is where I share the projects I'm proud of and what I'm learning as I go.</p>

